PLATFORMSSOUIAGENT(8)       System Manager's Manual      PLATFORMSSOUIAGENT(8)

NAME
     PlatformSSOUIAgent – Platform SSO User Interface Agent

DESCRIPTION
     PlatformSSOUIAgent is a system agent that provides user interface
     components for Platform SSO authentication. It manages authentication
     dialogs and credential collection for multiple authentication methods,
     operating in both standard user mode (as an agent) and system contexts.

     The agent operates in two modes: normal mode for standard user sessions,
     and login mode for FileVault unlock, OS installation, or migration
     scenarios. Login mode is activated automatically based on boot mode
     detection or by using the -l flag.

     The PlatformSSOUIAgent command should not be run directly.

OPTIONS
     -l      Force the agent to run in login mode.

FILES
     /System/Library/PrivateFrameworks/PlatformSSO.framework/Support/PlatformSSOUIAgent
             The agent executable

     /System/Library/LaunchAgents/com.apple.PlatformSSO.PlatformSSOUIAgent.plist
             Launch agent user session configuration

     /System/Library/LaunchAgents/com.apple.PlatformSSO.PlatformSSOUIAgent.login.plist
             Launch agent system session configuration

SEE ALSO
     launchd(8), log(1)

